  "prompt": "Are doctors' professional fees subject to VAT?",
  "runtimeCommit": "d71b913ddf39726234dd02d858fac3e5275e865b",
  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nAre doctors' professional fees subject to Value-Added Tax (VAT)?\n\n### Short Answer\nDoctors' professional fees are generally exempt from VAT under specific provisions of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\n### Practical Application\nIn practice, this means that doctors do not need to charge VAT on their professional fees when providing medical services. They should ensure that their billing reflects this exemption to avoid any potential issues with the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR). However, if a doctor engages in activities outside the scope of medical services or provides services that do not qualify for the exemption, those fees may be subject to VAT. It is advisable for medical professionals to maintain clear records and consult with tax professionals to ensure compliance with tax regulations.",
